eva: heads-up from sparrow-lite-q3 canary: streaming funcall parse failures ~2% across 8k calls; sync OK.
sam: is there a failing sample?
eva: captured chunks: ```
{"tool":"search","args":{"q":"sourdough"}}

{"tool":"open_url","args":{"url":"http://r.example/rec"}}

]}
```
tony: stray closing bracket ends up in new chunk, parser errors on suffix. likely tokenization boundary shift after quant kernel change.
ci-bot: canary start 1765439900 cfg=stream_chunk=512 kv_cache=on
eva: quick prototype: on streaming parse fail, attempt salvage by joining non-empty chunks with commas, wrap in array and json.loads. trial dropped failures to 0.5%.
sam: good improvement. worry about accidental merges changing tool order. add semantic-eval check and a safety rollback threshold.
tony: also add unit tests for truncated-suffix, controlchar-insert, and interleaved-tool-order. keep raw streams in audit log (redacted).
eva: rollout plan: land behind feature flag scoped to q3 quant families, enable canary-only for 24h, monitor parsed_tool_count and semantic-eval-delta, rollback if semantic score drops >0.5%.
